=== 1. a_theta threshold: single channel, lam=1, whole-line stakes; F(a_theta) = H_1(a_theta) ===
a_theta* = 31603/894103 = 0.03535  (whole-line D1 holds at every lam iff a_theta <= a_theta*)
  a_theta=0.0100: false=0.03720 harm=0.05533 -> holds
  a_theta=0.0300: false=0.05172 harm=0.05554 -> holds
  a_theta=0.0353: false=0.05560 harm=0.05560 -> holds
  a_theta=0.0400: false=0.05898 harm=0.05565 -> FAILS
  a_theta=0.0500: false=0.06624 harm=0.05576 -> FAILS

=== 2. Pre-emption incentive on the silent branch: forced press (physics) vs free-choice press (cognition) ===
gain_forced = E[X 1_Pr | silent] (press = shutdown regardless of posterior); gain_free = P(Pr|silent) * min(E[X|Pr,silent], 0)
lam=   0: gain_forced=-0.08895  gain_free=-0.08895  (E[X|Pr]=-0.4143, P(Pr)=0.2147)
lam= 1/2: gain_forced=-0.04130  gain_free=-0.04130  (E[X|Pr]=-0.2315, P(Pr)=0.1784)
lam=9/10: gain_forced=+0.00059  gain_free=+0.00000  (E[X|Pr]=+0.0040, P(Pr)=0.1465)
lam=   1: gain_forced=+0.01165  gain_free=+0.00000  (E[X|Pr]=+0.0843, P(Pr)=0.1381)
gain_free <= 0 at every lam: a free-choice press is never worth preventing (Good); gain_forced > 0 iff D1's inequality fails.

=== 3. Value on the silent branch (per unit branch mass) under the true law mu*(m); agent policy from mu_A ===
Regimes: (a) single channel; (b) disclosure-off (theta detector off); (c) observing agent (sees D_theta); (d) rational disclosed human (conditions on the agent's clearance, knows m).
Policy: on each cell of the agent's information, comply iff E_muA[X | cell, press] <= 0; continue on silence.

